dvantages throughout the trace, reinforcing the student’s correct reasoning trace. RefSol (bottom) produces diffuse negative advantages across the entire rollout: the teacher prefers the alternative derivation’s surface form even though the student’s answer is correct, mixing stylistic disagreement into the gradient.","image_text":[],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2606.11173v1-Figure3-1-6c2722f91362.png","asset_sha256":"6c2722f9136283acf51fdcbc9e5aca9864b80e896e021b8545546a909b52d653","metadata_sha256":"d705f789ca24e942d205d635577cee9b0807763b891edaebc0fc6313448eb49e"},{"artifact_id":"Figure4","kind":"figure","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"9b5f2341cae526105df68ad8cf1f703c6cebd9c396e7b8abe838db7ca8dd1d14","page_index":7,"region":{"x1":80.64,"y1":84.47999999999999,"x2":564.0,"y2":304.32},"caption_region":{"x1":81.60000610351562,"y1":315.6256103515625,"x2":563.4937744140625,"y2":357.7969665527344},"caption":"Figure 4 Incorrect step. Per-token advantages for a rollout containing an error at the step marked by the dashed line. StepAlignFB (top) produces a sharp negative shift at the tokens after the erroneous step, while reinforcing correct reasoning in the preceding steps. RefSol (bottom) produces broadly negative advantages across the entire trace, conflating the error with everywhere the student’s path diverges from the canonical solution.","image_text":[],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2606.11173v1-Figure4-1-b841fd13f8df.png","asset_sha256":"b841fd13f8dfb8416d18ac0a96d93cd972b8c6782352cc1513713c694fd6d449","metadata_sha256":"d705f789ca24e942d205d635577cee9b0807763b891edaebc0fc6313448eb49e"},{"artifact_id":"Figure5","kind":"figure","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"9b5f2341cae526105df68ad8cf1f703c6cebd9c396e7b8abe838db7ca8dd1d14","page_index":7,"region":{"x1":80.64,"y1":372.48,"x2":564.0,"y2":593.28},"caption_region":{"x1":81.60000610351562,"y1":604.0286254882812,"x2":563.6620483398438,"y2":646.200927734375},"caption":"Figure 5 Incomplete solution. Per-token advantages for a rollout that exhausted the token budget without producing a final answer. The student’s reasoning trace is unpromising from the start and quickly devolves into guessing values for the variable before running out of budget. The critic responds by producing a complete alternative solution, yielding update signals similar to those of the reference solution.","image_text":[],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2606.11173v1-Figure5-1-3c25b0d6388a.png","asset_sha256":"3c25b0d6388ab544cad5991fcad896941878484644bdb57113459dd26ee3a149","metadata_sha256":"d705f789ca24e942d205d635577cee9b0807763b891edaebc0fc6313448eb49e"},{"artifact_id":"Figure6","kind":"figure","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"9b5f2341cae526105df68ad8cf1f703c6cebd9c396e7b8abe838db7ca8dd1d14","page_index":8,"region":{"x1":80.64,"y1":504.48,"x2":564.0,"y2":612.9599999999999},"caption_region":{"x1":81.3499984741211,"y1":624.8436889648438,"x2":563.4912109375,"y2":655.0599975585938},"caption":"Figure 6 Full verbatim repetition with appended correction. The critic includes the student’s incorrect step verbatim and follows it with a textual correction. Induction-head copying of the original (incorrect) tokens dominates the teacher’s distribution; per-token advantages are overwhelmingly positive.","image_text":[],"render_dpi":150,"asset_path":"figures/fig_2606.11173v1-Figure6-1-85ca456cc76b.png","asset_sha256":"85ca456cc76b157a3d8bc3395cb62f1af11d1a3788c165ad13f52d81b485b2b8","metadata_sha256":"d705f789ca24e942d205d635577cee9b0807763b891edaebc0fc6313448eb49e"},{"artifact_id":"Figure7","kind":"figure","detector_name":"pdffigures2","detector_fingerprint":"pdffigures2-0.0.12-SNAPSHOT","source_pdf_sha256":"9b5f2341cae526105df68ad8cf1f703c6cebd9c396e7b8abe838db7ca8dd1d14","